  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Training-of-Trainers Sustainable Protected Cultivation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a training following the train-the-trainer principle for public and private extension officers and commercial farmers in Sri Lanka on sustainable protected cultivation. At the end of the training, participants can transfer the gained knowledge about the most relevant processes in protected cultivation, ranging from plant physiology to economics. Participants understand how technology affects climate management, crop production and resource use efficiency and can apply this knowledge.With the aim to:&#x2022;	increase yield, produce quality, and revenue;&#x2022;	increase water productivity, saving significant amounts of water, specifically relevant during the drought season;&#x2022;	significant reduction in pesticide use for lower production costs and healthier produce;&#x2022;	and more year-round production, allowing farmers to take advantage of market seasonality and higher prices.</narrative>
  </description>
